event('221-5.7-radicial','targeted proof check','A finite flat radicial X -> S has at most one point in each geometric fiber. For any section X_T -> Z and any point of T, the image of that finite fiber lies in one affine open of Z. The locus where the whole finite fiber maps into that open is open in T, since its complement is the finite image of a closed set. The affine restriction-of-scalars constructions therefore cover the section functor and glue as schemes. This checks why no quasi-projectivity restriction on Z is needed in the radicial case.','221, p. 273, opening continuation of 5.7')
event('221-jets','targeted proof check','With p_1:T_n -> T finite and flat as explicitly stipulated in the construction, its underlying map is radicial, so the preceding representability statement applies to p_2*X. Smoothness of X -> T survives the p_2 base change and then follows for the restriction of scalars from 5.7. The denominator must be T. Finiteness must be retained as a hypothesis here: for T=Spec k[x_1,x_2,...], the first principal-parts algebra has underlying module O_T plus Omega_T/k and is not finite. Thus no claim that arbitrary S-preschemes automatically have finite T_n is used in this check. For smooth T/S the principal-parts modules are locally finite free.','221, p. 273, jet-bundle paragraph')
event('221-6-affine-norm','targeted proof check','For affine S=Spec A and X=Spec B with the sheaf corresponding to a B-module M finite locally free of rank n over A, B tensor_A n acts on M tensor_A n. The invariant subalgebra TS_A^n(B) commutes with all permutations and therefore preserves the image of the antisymmetrization map from wedge^n M. That map is injective for locally free M, over any A, as checked in a basis: each increasing-index wedge has a distinct signed tensor orbit with coefficients plus or minus one. The preserved image is an invertible A-module, giving an A-algebra homomorphism TS_A^n(B) -> End_A(wedge^n M)=A and hence a section of the affine symmetric power. On b tensor ... tensor b its action is det(b on M). This supports the printed symmetric-power construction without requiring B to be flat over A, and does not justify the supplied divided-power rewrite.','221, p. 273, section 6 and last paragraph')
event('221-6-general-norm','carried as background without fault found','Read the asserted natural section for an arbitrary symmetric morphism u:(X/S)^n -> Y and the sufficient affine-orbit condition for existence of the symmetric quotient. The affine determinant construction was checked separately; a complete global construction for every stated X,Y,u has not been supplied here. The printed assertion is restored, without replacing it by a modern theorem with different hypotheses.','221, p. 273, section 6')
